<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>Kingdom Come, 2018</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;Saudi Arabia&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB style="FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; mso-ansi-language: EN-GB"&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;vs.&amp;nbsp;Egypt&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt; 
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB style="FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; mso-ansi-language: EN-GB"&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Date/Time:&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB style="mso-ansi-language: EN-GB"&gt; 18th&amp;nbsp;June 2018 / 01:00:00 Zulu&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = "o" ns = "urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;B style="mso-bidi-font-weight: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB style="mso-ansi-language: EN-GB"&gt;Location:&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB style="mso-ansi-language: EN-GB"&gt; &lt;?xml:namespace prefix = "st1" ns = "urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:smarttags" /&gt;&lt;st1:place w:st="on"&gt;Red Sea, Nile Valley and Sinai&lt;/st1:place&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB style="mso-ansi-language: EN-GB"&gt;&lt;st1:place w:st="on"&gt;&lt;/st1:place&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;B style="mso-bidi-font-weight: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB style="mso-ansi-language: EN-GB"&gt;Playable Sides:&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB style="mso-ansi-language: EN-GB"&gt; &lt;st1:country-region w:st="on"&gt;Saudi Arabia&lt;/st1:country-region&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB style="mso-ansi-language: EN-GB"&gt;&lt;st1:country-region w:st="on"&gt;&lt;/st1:country-region&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB style="mso-ansi-language: EN-GB"&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;B style="mso-bidi-font-weight: normal"&gt;&lt;U&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB style="mso-ansi-language: EN-GB"&gt;Introduction&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;B style="mso-bidi-font-weight: normal"&gt;&lt;U&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB style="mso-ansi-language: EN-GB"&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;Following an abortive assassination attempt on the King of Saudi Arabia, compelling links between the assassins and the Egyptian national intelligence agency, the&amp;nbsp;Mukhabarat, quickly came to light.&amp;nbsp; In the ensuing furor, diplomatic attempts to resolve the crisis between the two countries&amp;nbsp;failed as each side dug in their heels.&amp;nbsp; The Saudis would tolerate nothing less than having the responsible parties delivered to them immediately, while the Egyptians were still reeling from the realization that the Mukhabarat had initiated such an outrage without official sanction -&amp;nbsp;but to save face would not admit so.&amp;nbsp; With only hours to go before the deadline of the Saudi's ultimatum, the Egyptians came to the conclusion, under the circumstances,&amp;nbsp;that war was the more tenable option.&amp;nbsp; The Kingdom would ablige.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;U&gt;Scenario&amp;nbsp;Notes&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;This large scenario encompasses&amp;nbsp;a&amp;nbsp;48 hour opening surge of air/naval combat operations between Saudi Arabia and Egypt.&amp;nbsp; The Saudis possess a large, powerful and modern air force.&amp;nbsp; The Egyptians are modernizing, too, and have one of the most dangerous air defense networks in the world.&amp;nbsp; The Saudis must destroy their assigned targets to have a chance of victory.&amp;nbsp; Unfortunately these targets are heavily defended and time is short.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;The Egyptians have three squadrons of modern Rafale fighters, equipt with the Meteor AAM.&amp;nbsp; They also have two squadrons of modern MiG-29 Fulcrums and another two of updated Mirage 2000s (equivalent to the UAE Mirage 2000-9 model), all with competent air weapons.&amp;nbsp; The Egyptian F-16 fleet is sizable but depends on older AAMs such as the AIM-7M and AIM-9M.&amp;nbsp; Obsolescent aircraft are are also still in evidence.&amp;nbsp; A&amp;nbsp;handful of Hawkeye AEW aircraft provide overhead radar coverage.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;On the ground the older network of SA-2 and SA-3 systems are being phased out in lieu of more modern systems.&amp;nbsp; Batteries of SA-11, SA-17, Patriot and SA-23 systems have all been added in the past several years, backed by a robust system of powerful radars.&amp;nbsp; Reducing this system will be a formidable challenge.&amp;nbsp; Be cautious of their long-range SCUDs, as well.&amp;nbsp; While mainly a nuisance, a lucky hit can do a lot of damage.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;At sea the Egyptians have fielded new FREMM frigates, with capable air self defense and long range land-strike cruise missiles.&amp;nbsp; Additionally their new AIP Type 209 SSKs can pose a significant hazard to shipping.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;To keep the game somewhat playable the large amount of local shipping - coasters, fishing dhows, etc, have been removed.&amp;nbsp; It's assumed that this traffic still exists and is being monitored by&amp;nbsp;your forces.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;U&gt;Scoring&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;BR&gt;The Saudis begin with a substantial point deficit which can be erased by eliminating all the primary targets (in Cairo and Aswan, marked with [TARGET] name designators.&amp;nbsp; Points can also be made by eliminating Egyptian aircraft, naval assets, later-generation SAM systems and SCUD launchers.&amp;nbsp; Points are lost when Saudi aircraft go down, ships (including Saudi merchant vessels) are sunk and especially if any part of the Aswan Dam is destroyed (other than designated targets).&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
